 {:seon.task/name "a-run-whose-tree-changed-under-it-is-no-verdict"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by Optimization (2026-11-11): a run of onetree's seon.system-test was read as green after a tracked file was edited while it ran, and was discarded by hand. What exists: a `bin/test` shard compares the checkout's tree (```seon.fx/tree-id```) after its run with its plan's, and when they differ takes back the greens it wrote (```seon.fx/forget-greens!```), stores nothing and prints \"the tree changed since the plan: no result stored\" (test-runner/shard!), but the run's exit and its TEST OK stay as reported, so a session reads a green that judged no tree. Correct: a shard whose tree changed makes the run's last line INVALID (the tree it planned and the tree at its end) and its exit non-zero, as a died shard does; `bin/prove` and bin/check's runner read the same exit, so no caller reads it as green. Proof: a run whose test edits a tracked file of its checkout's tree ends INVALID with a non-zero exit, and stores nothing. docs/merging.md#verdicts-are-a-cache states it."
