  :seon.task/plan "Root's ruling, 2026-11-14 (asked by web): a test named in :seon.task/proofs of an OPEN task does not gate unrelated landings. It is open work, not a waived claim, and it gates only that task's done (the judge). So a red-first proof (principles 3: \"a proof never seen red\" is ruled out) never parks a branch.\n\nFound [M]: web's red proof seon.render-test/a-view-of-a-pulled-entity-is-matched-by-its-datom-keys (jolt/web 8ede7bdf2c, the proof of seon.ratom/a-view-of-a-pulled-entity-records-its-datom-keys) blocks every other web landing until the reaction core lands. Today bin/land fails on any red (bin/land:155, bin/prove's MERGE OK).\n\nChange: the merge's verdict leaves out the reds whose test is named only by open tasks' proofs. Each one is listed in the verdict as open work (task, test), never as green. A red of a test no open task names gates as today. The task's own done (seon.judge) still needs it green.\n- One place decides: the prove's plan, which already reads tasks.\n- No waiver key, so health's :no-waived-proof is untouched: the task names the test, and nothing else does.\n- Guard against abuse: a test that was green on main and is red on the branch still gates, because a regression is never open work. So only a test new on the branch, or red on main too, may be open.\n\nProof: seon.proofs-test/an-open-tasks-red-proof-leaves-the-merge-green. A branch adding a red test named by an open task proves green with it listed as open; the same red unnamed gates; and a test green on main turned red gates even when an open task names it.\n\nOwner: tests. Web filed it; web's branch is the first user.\n\nSharpened with tests-3:\n- \"Green on main\" means the verdict at main's own digest of that test, as reuse reads it, never any green ever.\n- A test main doesn't hold yet (a red-first proof new on the branch) has no verdict there, so it is open work.\n- The decision reads main's verdict, never the task's presence. So a red test whose digest the change moved, named by an open task the same change added, still gates if main held it green.\n- The proof covers that case too."
