 {:seon.task/name "a-verdict-reused-by-its-reads-covers-every-var-it-reaches"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-11-15 [M, tests-4]: seon.proofs-test/a-waived-pass-keeps-its-rows was reused green at its digest with test-runner/kept-report?, the function it asserts on, mutated to the old predicate; forced (bin/test --all) it went red. Its green's reads.edn recorded {the test var, seon.proofs/test-symbol, [:env], [:runner]}. The cause, read at both ends [M, tests-4 02:20]: seon.program/var-digests already folds into a test var's digest every var its call reaches that no contract counts (called-closure follows uncontracted refs: a data def, a macro, a test's helper), so a plain helper moves it; but the reach graph's contract map (seon.program reach-step's contract, from each var's :var/contract fact, contract-text of its :malli/schema meta) counts a var as contracted by its :malli/schema text alone, while a run records a call only of a var seon.contract/defn armed (its ::wrapper). test-runner/kept-report? is a clojure.core/defn with a :malli/schema map: the graph stops the closure there as \"recorded when called\", the run never records it, and the test is reused while it changes. Correct at the source, so the two notions are one: a :malli/schema on a function no contract arms is refused where the form is analyzed (or such a var's contract fact is not written), and the defns that hold one (test/test_runner.clj, about ninety in test/ namespaces that refer clojure.core's defn, render_test 52) take seon.contract/defn or drop the map; a law names any left. No :ucd digest is needed (tried and reverted: the closure already covers plain helpers). Estimate: one check a def at analysis. Proof, red first: a test calling an uncontracted helper is run again when the helper changes and reused when only an unrelated var does."
