e agent holding the branch, items, batches granted by the :process effect owner's admission); the agent's forked test children (seon.agent/run-tests-forked, fork-test-child, the fold test-run-step, child-ended); the fork server's one fork (seon.lib/fork!, seon.fork-server); bin/test and bin/prove, test/test_runner.clj, a cold process per run with its own plan and file cache (frozen, AGENTS.md section 0.5); the binary's identity, seon.fx/runtime-for and seon.system/binary-current, two checks deps' part 2 makes one; baked paths, seon.system/baked-changes. So E builds nothing beside: bin/test and bin/prove become thin clients of :prove (bin/mcp call prove, the existing op), and a test runs where an agent's run already does, in a child forked from the standing system. MEASURED [root result/b0ba08fb]: of 2,197 tests, 1,928 run in a fork (88%), 240 reach the binary, 29 a process of their own. [result/c4304ba8]: of today's 96 lands on main, 34 changed a path only a build carries (seon.system/baked-changes): 14 schema paths, 2 pins, 1 config, system.edn; if schemas load in place as forms do (deps and runtime to judge), ~4 lands rerun binary tests. bin/test's own start [M 17:02, load 8.6, /tmp/tests4/split.log]: one reused test answered in 71 s wall (37 s user, 28 s sys), selection 3.2 s and ~66 s before its plan's first store read (build check, libraries, process boot), for no test run; root measured ~0.98 s a test outside its own work over 267k runs. COST of E: a test run through :prove pays no process start (the standing system is warm), its plan reads the store's verdicts (the cleanup land), its child a fork (~65 ms, docs/cost.md) and the test's own ticks (median under 16M, ~0.1 s); a land's run of n tests ~ n x (65 ms + its work) / workers, against today's 0.98 s each plus ~66 s a process. Binary tests run on the candidate system the new binary boots beside the standing one (the owner's idea), keyed on its identity: only lands that change what a build carries run them. 